          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Huc, custos, igitur pervigil advola, avertens patria de tibi credita tam morbos animi, quam requiescere quidquid non sinit incolas.",
          "english": "Then, watchful Guardian, spread thy wings and cleave the air, haste hither to our home committed to thy care; drive thence each noxious ill that might the soul infest, nor suffer danger here to rest.",
          "sourcePages": [
            413
          ],
          "englishPages": [
            413,
